 Muslim society and culture. The rulers took lead in the celebration of religious rites and festivities and thus strengthened the religious feeling of the Muslim Community. They sent presents to the holy cities of Makkah and Madinah and provided facilities to the people to go to the Hajj. The rulers observed the Islamic Law in the conduct of the state. They owed allegiance to the \'Abbasid caliphs of Baghdad and maintained connections with the Islamic world. These worked for the solidarity of the Muslims and the development of the Muslim culture in Bengal.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 929, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 813})
