d caliph Yazid I, massacred Ali’s son Husayn along with seventy-two of his companions and family members (that number has since symbolized martyrdom). Husayn’s refusal to the legitimacy of the Umayyad caliphate had been a stance that he shared with the people of Kufa, Ali’s capital.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 900, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 865})
